<title>USA: Foster Wheeler incinerator suit dismissed.</title>
<headline>Foster Wheeler incinerator suit dismissed.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. District Court judge in Chicago Friday dismissed a lawsuit against Illinois officials brought by Foster Wheeler Corp, developer of a bond-financed incinerator in Robbins, Ill.</p>
<p>Judge James Zagel dismissed the suit on the ground that the 11th amendment to the U.S. Constitution precludes lawsuits dealing with public funds. Lawyers for Illinois officials had asked the judge to dismiss the case on that basis.</p>
</text>
